  "conclusions": [
    "Six day columns are honest from 90rem (1440px) up: the board is 888px and each day is 147px, holding a Task card whose title measures 73px over up to three lines.",
    "At 1280 six columns would be 108px, which the card cannot hold \u2014 so the board FOLDS to three columns over two rows (230px each) rather than shrinking. Recompose, never squeeze.",
    "The queue rail gives up 2rem (21rem to 19rem) only at the six-column width, and every pixel of it lands on the day columns.",
    "No document scrolls sideways at 1440, 1280, 820, 393 or 320, on either surface."
  ]
